      "number": 111,
      "sectionId": "dai",
      "sectionName": "Data Analysis & Interpretation",
      "stimulusId": null,
      "text": "Directions: In the following question, two quantities I and II are given. Compare quantity I and quantity II on its basis. (Only quantity is to be considered). Two series A and B are given below with one wrong term in series. A: 3, 8, 24, 45, 120, 168 B: 28, 42, 56, 98, 154, 182 Quantity I: Average of wrong terms of both the series. Quantity II: Difference between the next term of series A and the next term of series B.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Quantity I > Quantity II"
        },
        {
          "text": "Quantity I < Quantity II"
        },
        {
          "text": "Quantity I ≥ Quantity II"
        },
        {
          "text": "Quantity I ≤ Quantity II"
        },
        {
          "text": "Quantity I = Quantity II or No relation"
        }
      ],
