        }
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "explanation": "Under Basel III, the minimum Common Equity Tier 1 (CET1) capital requirement for banks in India is 8%. Regulators may impose a capital conservation buffer, typically set at 2.5% of RWAs, to ensure banks build up capital during periods of economic stability that can be used during periods of stress. Banks are required to maintain a minimum CET1 ratio of 5.5% of risk-weighted asset. In addition to the minimum CET1 requirement, banks should also maintain a CCB of 2.5% of RWAs, also in the form of CET1 capital.",
